i-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:4ef626fe792b60714635feff34aaacb3688ae345af9ddd67f036182c847d3fb5","file":"preprints/The-low-temperature-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-free-energy-limiting-law-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":277,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"51885987e08f233e0d94911513c922ea0ee38a54349223a3b9a47308a8fbf45a","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-low-temperature-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-free-energy-limiting-law-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:4ef626fe792b60714635feff34aaacb3688ae345af9ddd67f036182c847d3fb5","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-low-temperature-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-free-energy-limiting-law-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L277"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:skcw}\nFix $\\beta>1$ and $0\\le\\gamma<1$. Using the same independent standard\nGaussian couplings as in \\eqref{eq:model}, define the exponent and log\npartition function\n\\[\n \\begin{gathered}\n \\mathcal H_n^{\\mathrm{CW}}(\\sigma;\\beta,\\gamma)\n =\n \\frac{\\beta}{\\sqrt n}\\sum_{1\\le i<j\\le n}g_{ij}\\sigma_i\\sigma_j\n +\\frac{\\gamma}{2n}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n\\sigma_i\\right)^2,\\\\\n F_n^{\\mathrm{CW}}(\\beta,\\gamma)\n =\\log\\sum_{\\sigma\\in\\{-1,1\\}^n}\n e^{\\mathcal H_n^{\\mathrm{CW}}(\\sigma;\\beta,\\gamma)}.\n \\end{gathered}\n\\]\nHere $\\gamma$ is the ferromagnetic coupling already in the exponent.\nAs $n\\to\\infty$ through all integers,\n\\[\n \\begin{gathered}\n \\Var F_n^{\\mathrm{CW}}(\\beta,\\gamma)\n \\sim a_2(\\beta)n^{1/3},\\\\\n \\frac{F_n^{\\mathrm{CW}}(\\beta,\\gamma)\n       -\\mathbb E F_n^{\\mathrm{CW}}(\\beta,\\gamma)}\n      {\\sqrt{\\Var F_n^{\\mathrm{CW}}(\\beta,\\gamma)}}\n \\Longrightarrow\\nu_\\beta.\n \\end{gathered}\n\\]\nHere $a_2(\\beta)>0$ is the constant $a_2$ above at the same $\\beta$.\nThe centering and standard deviation are the perturbed model's own\nexact finite-size quantities."}
